-#      hollow border-4 sprite near the right side fills with 7.
-#    Original logic would collapse everything into one mapping and cannot
-#    disambiguate shared keys; the variant therefore changes the palette-read
-#    stage and the sprite-to-palette assignment stage.
-#
+#    The input now contains two separate palette blocks on two different edges.
+#    One palette is horizontal on the top or bottom edge; the other is vertical on
+#    the left or right edge. Each palette still uses the old edge-dependent
+#    reading direction locally, but the solver must detect and read both in the
+#    same grid. Example trace:
